  "prediction": "The report outlines the establishment and purpose of the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress, which was created by the House of Representatives in January 2019 to investigate ways to improve congressional operations. The committee, composed of equal numbers of Democrats and Republicans, was given the mandate to investigate various aspects of congressional procedures and make recommendations for modernization. The committee's authorizing resolution established its procedures and provided funding for its operations. The committee held several hearings, the first of which was to gather suggestions from members of Congress on potential areas for improvement. Subsequent hearings featured testimony from experts and practitioners on various topics related to congressional operations. The committee is required to submit a final report with its findings and recommendations to the House by the end of its term, which is scheduled for February 2020. The report must be made publicly available within 24 hours of each meeting and any recommendations must be made public within 30 days of submission to the House. The committee has been provided with funding and access to House resources to carry out its work.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report outlines the establishment and purpose of the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress, which was created by the House of Representatives in January 2019 to investigate ways to improve congressional operations. The committee, composed of equal numbers of Democrats and Republicans, was given the mandate to investigate various aspects of congressional procedures and make recommendations for modernization. The committee's authorizing resolution established its procedures and provided funding for its operations. The committee held several hearings, the first of which was to gather suggestions from members of Congress on potential areas for improvement. Subsequent hearings featured testimony from experts and practitioners on various topics related to congressional operations. The committee is required to submit a final report with its findings and recommendations to the House by the end of its term, which is scheduled for February 2020. The report must be made publicly available within 24 hours of each meeting and any recommendations must be made public within 30 days of submission to the House. The committee has been provided with funding and access to House resources to carry out its work.",
  "score": 36.286919337712966,
  "answers": [
    "On January 4, 2019, the House established the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress by adopting Title II of H.Res. 6, the House rules package for the 116th Congress (2019-2020), on a 418-12 vote. The purpose of the select committee as stated in its authorizing resolution is \"to investigate, study, make findings, hold public hearings, and develop recommendations on modernizing Congress.\" Twelve Members, six from each party, have been selected by their leadership to serve on the select committee during its year-long investigation. The committee's authorizing resolution requires its membership to include two Members from the freshman class of the 116th Congress, two Members of the Rules Committee, and two Members of the Committee on House Administration. Funding for the select committee in the amount of $487,500 was provided through House adoption of H.Res. 245 on March 27, 2019. The committee has held four hearings to date, with additional meetings likely. Committee operations are scheduled to end on February 1, 2020. Any final report of the committee will be made public. Publication of the final report will require approval from at least two-thirds of the committee. Given that both parties are equally represented on the committee, some amount of bipartisan support will be needed to approve and publish the final report."
  ],
